            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="BLA04" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>William</forename>
                        <surname>Blackwood</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1776-11-20">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1834-09-16"/>
                    <occupation>publisher</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Blackwood was the publisher and founder of <title>Blackwood's Edinburgh Magazine</title>. After completing his apprenticeship, he worked for some time 
      in London before returning to Edinburgh to start his own business in 1804. He began publishing <title>Blackwood's Edinburgh Magazine</title> in 1817 and it 
      proved highly successful as well as controversial.</p>
                        <p>Identification is confirmed through a letter from William Blackwood 
    to <persName key="SHE02">Mary Shelley</persName> dated 24 April 1830, sending her a copy of the magazine with a notice for <title>Cloudesley</title> in it and 
    saying that he had a great respect for Mr Godwin and had come to know him personally 
    at the dinner parties given by <persName key="JOH02">Mr Johnson</persName>. Blackwood's association with Johnson corresponds with one of the diary references.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="MS"> MS. Abinger c. 48, fols. 69-70: 24 April 1830</bibl>
                    <bibl type="MS"> MS. Abinger c. 20, fol. 23: 1 June 1830</bibl>
                    <bibl type="MS"> MS. Abinger c. 20, fol. 24: 10 June 1830</bibl>
                    <bibl type="MS"> MS. Abinger c. 14, fol.12: 24 February 1832</bibl>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>DNB</title>
                    </bibl>
                </person>
